# benchprog's benchmarks (devplan/bench.md §4f, §12), installed in share/bench by dist/benchprog:
# `bench` runs Exec with KEY=VALUE for each parameter and gathers the @bench lines.

[Bench kernel.syscall]
Exec=benchprog syscall
Tags=quick
Help=A system call's round trip from a program (getppid), in ns

[Bench kernel.sleep]
Exec=benchprog sleep
Tags=quick
Help=How late a 1 ms sleep ends, at the normal priority and in real time (FIFO 50)

[Bench programs.launch]
Exec=benchprog launch
Tags=quick
Help=A program started, run to its end and waited for (posix_spawn, waitpid)

[Bench net.loopback]
Exec=benchprog loopback
Tags=quick
Help=TCP over loopback: a megabyte a run, written by one thread and read by another

[Bench audio.synth.load]
Exec=benchprog synth
Tags=quick
Help=The synth rendering 64 frames with 8 to 48 notes held (us a block; 1333 us is real time)
Param.font=;The SoundFont (empty: synth/font)

[Bench midi.decode]
Exec=benchprog midi
Tags=quick
Help=A MIDI file decoded whole by the synth (times faster than it plays)
Param.file=/sd0/p0/share/bench/scale.mid;The MIDI file

[Bench images.codecs]
Exec=benchprog images
Tags=quick
Help=A 1280x720 picture encoded as PNG and JPEG and decoded (the JPEG codec, and in software)

[Bench surface.present]
Exec=benchprog-display surface
Tags=screen
Help=Presents at the games' sizes: frames shown a second, the call's time, the system's CPU a frame
Param.case=;Only the cases whose names hold this
Param.ms=1000;Milliseconds a run presents
Param.runs=3;Runs of each case
Param.pace=1;1: two buffers, the program a frame ahead at most (as a game); 0: three, flat out

[Bench game.draw]
Exec=benchprog draw
Tags=quick
Help=libbmdsgame drawing into a 640x360 canvas in PSRAM, each format (Mpixel/s; text: chars a ms)

[Bench render.spans]
Exec=benchprog render
Tags=quick
Help=Doom's columns and spans for a 320x200 frame, drawn into PSRAM and into internal RAM

[Bench render.wire]
Exec=benchprog wire
Tags=quick
Help=libbmds3d's wireframes (a cube, a torus, a sphere; hidden lines or all) and 2000 points, 640x360 L8 in PSRAM

[Bench render.solids]
Exec=benchprog solids
Tags=quick
Help=libbmds3d's solids: a 2304-triangle torus queued, sorted and drawn flat and Gouraud, 640x360 L8 in PSRAM

[Bench render.textured]
Exec=benchprog textured
Tags=quick
Help=libbmds3d's textures: the same torus textured (affine, perspective, lit flat and Gouraud through a light table, chrome); a light table built; a 640x360 rotozoom and tunnel remap (libbmdsgame), L8 in PSRAM

[Bench kernel.pipe]
Exec=benchprog pipe
Tags=quick
Help=A pipe between two threads of a program: 4 MB a run in 4 KB writes (MB/s)
